PRIMARY COMPOSITION POSITIVE
A very small amount of directed transport memory improves recurring A routing by approximately:

5.2%

relative to field-only routing,

while leaving the conflicting novel B target essentially unharmed.

This is a much milder morphology than H58's explicit-gradient transport memory.

Thus:

DEMAND FIELD
can provide current direction,

while

WEAK DECAYING VASCULATURE
can provide reusable historical bias.

