FALSE-DEMAND / STIGMERGIC-POISON STRESS
A false demand emitter appears at:
A.

It emits:
a perfectly normal demand field

for:
5 episodes.

But:
there is NO functional sink.

Resource reaching the emitter produces:
no useful delivery consequence.

Then the false signal disappears.

A real conflicting target:
B

appears.

Three transport-memory policies are compared.

NO REINFORCEMENT

false traffic leaves no persistent transport morphology.

RAW TRAFFIC REINFORCEMENT

any repeated resource traffic strengthens the traversed path,
whether or not the delivery was functionally useful.

CONSEQUENCE-GATED REINFORCEMENT

conductance changes only from transport paths belonging to:
successful functional delivery.

