DECISION
AR-H59 is POSITIVE WITH A CONSEQUENCE-GATING REQUIREMENT.

Supported synthetically:

- purely local diffusive demand signal can route resource without target coordinates;
- longer signal propagation improves reach at a real locality/latency cost;
- multiple simultaneous demand sources coexist in one field;
- weak directed decaying vasculature improves recurring demand without materially harming novelty;
- overly strong transport memory can override correct current demand;
- false demand can poison transport morphology if raw traffic reinforces paths;
- functional-delivery gating prevents that false-path write in the tested stress.

Not demonstrated:

- real target-free demand emission;
- asynchronous field propagation;
- noisy / adversarial demand emitters mixed with real ones;
- demand-source trust;
- functional uptake signal on current Yggdrasil;
- interaction with conserved H56 activation credits in one full model.

